From 032f0bd0d9008aa5e0772103929e26a84d26dd79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 07:52:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add missing Google Calendar UI to provider dashboard

The backend calendar-sync routes (/api/calendar/connect, /status,
/disconnect) and their JS event listeners already existed, but the
actual button/status markup they were looking for
(#connectCalendarBtn, #disconnectCalendarBtn, #calendarStatusText)
was never added to dashboard.html's rendered content. The old
listeners also ran on DOMContentLoaded, before the dashboard content
(built dynamically by initDashboard() in script.js) even existed in
the DOM, so they always no-op'd.

- script.js: add a 'Google Calendar Sync' card to the dashboard
  render (status text + connect/disconnect buttons). Wire up
  checkCalendarStatus() and the button click handlers immediately
  after the dashboard HTML is inserted into the DOM, so the elements
  actually exist when the listeners attach. Show a success toast and
  clean up the URL when redirected back from Google's OAuth flow
  (?calendar=connected).
- dashboard.html: remove the dead duplicate calendar wiring that ran
  on DOMContentLoaded and never worked, now that the real wiring
  lives in initDashboard().
---
 frontend/dashboard.html | 76 ++-------------------------------
 frontend/script.js      | 93 +++++++++++++++++++++++++----------------
 2 files changed, 60 insertions(+), 109 deletions(-)

